    scv_distributed_textual_db_missing_production_boundaries_2026-09-13, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: the doc's actionable item was the unsafe write/allocation path in src/lib/scv/metadata_db.spl (SdnDatabase+WAL store): SdnTable.add_row always appends+repoints the index yet ScvMetaDb.insert/insert_batch had NO admission check - re-inserting a settled first-column key silently clobbered it, and next_key derived keys purely from tv.rows.len() so a non-sequential key occupying the count-based candidate would be re-allocated (must never allocate a settled alias). The doc's :117 perf item and network_remote/test_db_compat items are the L0-L10 feature program the triage addenda explicitly scope out of a P3 lane. Fix: insert refuses (false) when the primary key is already settled, checked BEFORE the WAL append so a refused write leaves no trace; insert_batch applies the same per-item preflight plus within-batch duplicate refusal, whole batch rejected with no WAL write; next_key scans upward past any settled candidate (fv_1, fv_2 normal case unchanged); read paths untouched, no API signature changed, no any, zero warnings naming the touched files. Spec test/02_integration/app/scv_metadata_db_spec extended (duplicate single insert refused with settled row + WAL intact; next_key skip over a settled count-based candidate; batch rejected wholesale for re-settling and intra-batch duplication) 6/6 PASS; neighbours scv_metadata_batch 8/8, scv_symbol_entity 3/3 PASS. Residuals per doc (L0-L10 program, not this lane): per-insert read-modify-write of the whole SdnDatabase remains (TODO perf; batch bounds it to one copy per batch); network_remote auth (Token/OAuth2/SigV4) + resumable transfer remain documented stubs; test_db_compat lacks the REQ-016..021 revision model; the design-only system spec and its fail-fast checkers untouched. close_evidence reproducer=test/02_integration/app/scv_metadata_db_spec.spl prevention=test/02_integration/app/scv_metadata_batch_spec.spl"

